                        <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_847">Gawsworth, Cheshire.
                                Parish church of St James</orgName>
                            <p>Kalendar, March 17: <q>Obitus d<ex>omi</ex>ni <persName>Georgii
                                        Baguley</persName> Rectoris istius Ecclesie Anno domini Mᵒ
                                    cccc nonagesimo septimo litera dominicalis A</q>; elsewhere
                                obits of <persName>Thomas Fyton</persName> 1494 and of
                                    <persName>Robert Fyton</persName> 1495 are added in the same
                                hand, and obits of other members of the Fyton family in other later
                                hands. For George Baguley, Rector of Gawsworth (of which the Fytons
                                were patrons), see George Ormerod, <title>The history of the county
                                    palatine and city of Chester, Volume 3</title> (1819), p. 294.
                                William Durham Rector of Tredington gave a Tredington document A.D.
                                1504, inserted as pp. v-vi, but there is no evidence that he gave
                                the missal.</p></provenance>
                    </history>
